              "id": "CVE-2019-14232",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Django: backtracking in a regular expression in django.utils.text.Truncator leads to DoS"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "An issue was discovered in Django 1.11.x before 1.11.23, 2.1.x before 2.1.11, and 2.2.x before 2.2.4. If django.utils.text.Truncator's chars() and words() methods were passed the html=True argument, they were extremely slow to evaluate certain inputs due to a catastrophic backtracking vulnerability in a regular expression. The chars() and words() methods are used to implement the truncatechars_html and truncatewords_html template filters, which were thus vulnerable."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "error"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-14232",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2019-14232\nSeverity: HIGH\nPackage: Django\nFixed Version: 1.11.23, 2.1.11, 2.2.4\nLink: [CVE-2019-14232](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-14232)\nAn issue was discovered in Django 1.11.x before 1.11.23, 2.1.x before 2.1.11, and 2.2.x before 2.2.4. If django.utils.text.Truncator's chars() and words() methods were passed the html=True argument, they were extremely slow to evaluate certain inputs due to a catastrophic backtracking vulnerability in a regular expression. The chars() and words() methods are used to implement the truncatechars_html and truncatewords_html template filters, which were thus vulnerable.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2019-14232**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|HIGH|Django|1.11.23, 2.1.11, 2.2.4|[CVE-2019-14232](https://avd.aquasec.com/nvd/cve-2019-14232)|\n\nAn issue was discovered in Django 1.11.x before 1.11.23, 2.1.x before 2.1.11, and 2.2.x before 2.2.4. If django.utils.text.Truncator's chars() and words() methods were passed the html=True argument, they were extremely slow to evaluate certain inputs due to a catastrophic backtracking vulnerability in a regular expression. The chars() and words() methods are used to implement the truncatechars_html and truncatewords_html template filters, which were thus vulnerable."
              },
